Found under k22. _remote_urls in lib/Dist/Zilla/PluginBundle/Author/GETTY.pm runs git through backticks with single-quoted arguments and 2>/dev/null, which cmd.exe does not understand; on native Windows the remote list is then probably always empty, so a GitHub dist would get no_github = 1 and no GithubMeta. Not verified on Windows. Check on a windows-latest probe and, if real, run git with a list form (no shell) instead.

2026-11-10 01:51 Fix in tree: _remote_urls (bundle) and GiteaMeta _build_remote_info run git through a list-form pipe open (no shell), STDERR dup'ed to File::Spec->devnull for the call and restored; one private _git_output helper per module (no new module). Linux: prove -lr green (37 files/1073), dogfood dzil build META still GitHub via origin. Linux repro of the old GiteaMeta form: a remote named x'&%PATH% -> 'sh: Syntax error: Unterminated quoted string' on STDERR, _remote_info undef; new form reads it. Next: windows-latest probe workflow (scratch, not in repo).

